+\subsection{Inference and its scope}
+Paired non-circular moving blocks \citep{Kunsch1989} generate 5,000 resamples, seed 20261113, length 20 primary and 10/60 sensitivity. Percentile intervals condition on saved predictions, do not refit models, and are not multiplicity adjusted. They concern reversible-minus-unrestricted and unrestricted-minus-IID differences; an interval containing zero does not establish equivalence. These intervals summarize variability of paired realized losses or returns in the saved forecast evaluation, under the dependence assumptions of block resampling. They do not regenerate threshold estimation, parameter estimation or design selection across new histories. Parameter estimation can affect forecast-evaluation inference \citep{West1996}; no general coverage result is asserted here for the expanding-window, moving-threshold procedure. Block-length sensitivity does not by itself resolve structural change. SPY is the primary application, while the multiple metrics and related-ETF comparisons remain pointwise evidence rather than a familywise or independent-replication claim.
 
